  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "3 v 3 intervals – stop the ball on the line",
  "description": "Mark out a limited area with four cones, for example across the rink on both sides of the centre line. Two teams of three play each other. Each team attacks the opponents' end of the area and scores by stopping the ball on the line between the cones.\n\nPlay three minutes at a high tempo, rest for one minute and go again – 5–6 rounds in total. During the rest the players drink and the coach gives a short instruction. With more players, run several areas at the same time.\n\nRules to vary: a maximum of three touches per player, or everyone in the team must have been over the centre line before the point counts. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The whole team works all the time – show yourself for a pass or win the ball back."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Move the ball quickly to the free player instead of dribbling into the defenders."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "When you lose the ball: the nearest player presses at once, the others cover the passing lanes."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Keep the area wide – do not have three players in the same spot."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "phase": "game",
  "difficulty": 3,
